{"name":"Chic Shade","hex":"#7c9270","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"chic","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Elegant, stylish."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Good form; style.","A person with (a particular type of) chic."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/chic"},{"term":"shade","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Darkness where light, particularly sunlight, is blocked.","Something that blocks light, particularly in a window."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To shield (someone or something) from light.","To shield oneself from light."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/shade"}],"entries":[{"title":"Chic","blocks":[{"text":"Chic, meaning \"stylish\" or \"smart\", is an element of fashion. It was originally a French word."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chic"},{"title":"Tint, shade and tone","blocks":[{"text":"In color theory, a tint is a mixture of a color with white, which increases lightness, while a shade is a mixture with black, which increases darkness. A tone is produced either by mixing a color with gray, or by both tinting and shading. Mixing a color with any neutral color reduces the chroma, or colorfulness, while the perceived hue can be affected slightly."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d6/Tint-tone-shade.svg/330px-Tint-tone-shade.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tint%2C_shade_and_tone"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/0/0a/Monte_Carlo_Casino_2.JPG/500px-Monte_Carlo_Casino_2.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/0/0a/Monte_Carlo_Casino_2.JPG/500px-Monte_Carlo_Casino_2.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Riviera chic – Monte Carlo.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3A